      "description": "Watch Barracas Central vs Aldosivi highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 29, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina continued its relentless pace on July 29, 2026, as Barracas Central squared off against Aldosivi . Both teams arrived with a clear tactical plan, looking to secure vital points in a mid-season clash defined by narrow margins and high physical demand. Porra Strikes Before the Break The first half was a tactical battle, with clear-cut chances proving difficult to come by as both defenses stood tall. The deadlock was finally broken in the 40th minute through a moment of pure clinical execution. Ivan Tapia , acting as the creative hub for Barracas Central , delivered a perfectly weighted assist to Tomas Porra , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net. This crucial breakthrough changed the complexion of the match, allowing the home side to head into the interval with a slim but deserved lead. Tactical Shifts and Late Discipline Seeking an equalizer, Aldosivi made significant changes at the start of the second half, introducing Martin Garcia and Matias Godoy . The match grew increasingly heated as the clock ticked down, leading to a flurry of disciplinary actions. Rafael Barrios was cautioned for the hosts, while Aldosivi saw Martin Garcia and later Andres Chavez enter the referee’s book. Barracas Central managed the final stages by rotating their personnel, bringing on the likes of Rodrigo Bogarin and Maximiliano Puig to see out the result. Despite late pressure from the visitors and several substitutions aimed at salvaging a point, including the introduction of Andres Vombergar and Gonzalo Maroni , Barracas Central held firm. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+5 minutes, confirming a hard-fought 1-0 victory for the hosts in a game where defensive discipline and one clinical finish proved to be the difference."
